# THE SIFREI ROWS on Numbers 15:1-31 (THE NUMBERS WALK sitting 4 — SHELACH, 2026-09-10): piskaot 107-112 by POSITION, 12 rows at the
# shelf's row grain, each opened and verdicted; the middah named where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md: I1 a-fortiori, I2 the
# identity of wording, I3 the paradigm / prototype, I4-I7 general-particular, I8 the exemplar departing from the general to teach,
# I13 two verses reconciled by a third). The Sifrei has NO ROW on chapters 13-14 (asserted in shelach_ink.py — the spies and the decree
# read on Onkelos alone); piska 110's head "15:15-17" is placed at 15:17 by position and its opening words (a fourth mistyped head).
from shelach_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

# ---- piska 107 (15:2-13): the libations — who brings them, for which offerings, in what measure ----
srow(107, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'LIBATIONS AFTER INHERITANCE AND SETTLEMENT; THE OFFERINGS THAT TAKE THEM. "When you come to the land of your SETTLINGS" (15:2 — the word\'s one Numbers seat at this clause; computed): R. Yishmael — obligated only after inheritance and settlement, from Deut 17:14\'s specified "coming" ("and you inherit it and you settle in it") read onto every unqualified "coming" (I8: the one specified instance teaches the class); R. Akiva\'s objection — the Sabbath too is written "settlings" (Lev 23:3) and obtains everywhere; the reply an a-fortiori (I1: if the lighter commands obtain outside the land, the graver Sabbath the more so) — and "settlings" then teaches that a private altar (bamah) takes no libations; R. Akiva: it teaches that libations ARE offered on a bamah — a DISPUTE on the same word. Abba Chanan in R. Eliezer\'s name: the Temple\'s vessels exceeded the tent\'s (1 Kgs 7:27) but its libations did not (15:2-3). THE CENSUS OF "A FIRE-OFFERING" (15:3): every fire-offering would take libations, even a meal-offering — "a burnt-offering" limits; "a sacrifice" adds the peace-offerings, "or a sacrifice" the thanksgiving; the vow-and-gift clause EXCLUDES firstborn, tithe, Passover and guilt-offering; "or in your festivals" RE-INCLUDES the mandatory festival offerings; and the bull of 15:8 "was in the general category and departed to teach about the category" (I8): as the bull comes for vow or gift, all that come for vow or gift take libations — sin- and guilt-offerings excluded. (The export renders "or in gift" as "or as a guilt-offering" at one point — the shelf\'s translation slip, the ink\'s בִנְדָבָה ("in a freewill offering") standing; recorded.) The exam: Mishnah Menachot 9 and 12; Zevachim 14 (the bamah).')
srow(107, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE FOWL EXCLUDED; ONE KIND SUFFICES; THE MEASURES BY THE BEAST; ON BOWLS, NOT ON THE FIRE; THE MIXING RULE. "Of the herd or of the flock" (15:3): R. Yoshiyah — excludes the fowl burnt-offering from libations (I4-I5: the particular after the general); R. Yochanan — "a sacrifice" already limits to a beast, so the clause teaches that one who vowed a burnt-offering brings EITHER kind by itself (against Lev 1:2\'s "from the herd and from the flock" — the ink writes AND at Leviticus and OR here: computed in the ledger\'s ink section); the Passover\'s "from the sheep and from the goats" decided by an a-fortiori from the graver burnt-offering (I1); Issi b. Akiva\'s FOUR-ROUND REFUTATION CHAIN — the Shavuot lambs, the Yom Kippur goats, the sin-offering each proposed as the paradigm and each refuted by "Scripture expanding / limiting its bringing" until the verse itself decides (the common-side test — the shared-facet paradigm — run to exhaustion, then the ink — I3 refused thrice and closed by the clause). "The one who brings shall bring" (15:4) — a woman too; R. Nathan\'s PROTOTYPE: no donated meal-offering less than an issaron (I3); oil for mixing, wine for libation; "with the burnt-offering OR the sacrifice" — one libation PER offering, not per vow of five; Abba Chanan\'s a-fortiori (the ox and the lamb alike burned yet unlike in libations) answered by the clause; R. Nathan — the leper\'s burnt-, sin- and guilt-offerings take libations though mandatory; "for each lamb" — the woman after birth, and THE ELEVENTH (the tithe\'s mis-count) included, "for nowhere in the Torah is the secondary severer than the primary"; THE TABLE (15:4-11): the lamb a quarter hin, the ram a third, the bull a half — differentiated for lamb and ram (against the a-fortiori that would equate them from the undifferentiated calf and ox), NOT differentiated for calf and ox ("the ONE ox" — big or small), nor for a two- and three-year ram ("the ONE ram"), nor ewe-lamb and ewe ("the lamb among the sheep"), and the largest goat equated with the youngest lamb ("or among the goats" — three logs); the omer\'s lamb with two esronim but a single libation against the ram\'s doubled both (Lev 23:13 — the parser reads its 2; computed); "for libations" (15:10) — ON BOWLS, for wine on the fire would quench it against Lev 6:6\'s perpetual fire (I13: two verses reconciled — the reading forced by a third); "thus shall you do for each one" (15:12) — the EXCHANGES (temurah) included; "according to their number" — no decrease, and no increase either (R. Yoshiyah), or R. Yonah: "all the native-born shall do thus" already bars both and the clause bars the DOUBLED gift — whence THE MIXING RULE: bulls\' with rams\', lambs\' with lambs\', individuals\' with the congregation\'s, today\'s with yesterday\'s, but never lambs\' with bulls\' and rams\' (their numbers differ) — Mishnah Menachot 9\'s row on this clause. The exam: Menachot 9, 12-13; Zevachim 8, 10.')
srow(107, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'LIBATIONS DONATED — THREE LOGS AND UP, NEVER TWO OR FIVE; THE GENTILE\'S BURNT-OFFERING. "All the native-born shall do thus" (15:13): libations may be DONATED alone; the minimum three logs (a lamb\'s quarter hin); "shall do" — he may add; "thus" — not less: whence "one does not donate two or five, but three, four, six or above" (the amounts that exactly suffice for some beast — Mishnah Menachot 12:4\'s row). Variantly: Lev 22:25\'s "from the hand of a gentile" admits his unblemished burnt-offering — then "all the native-born" says an Israelite brings libations and a gentile does not; yet "shall do thus" — his burnt-offering still REQUIRES them: "if a gentile sent his burnt-offering from abroad with libations, his are used; if not, the congregation brings them" — Mishnah Shekalim 7:6\'s row on this clause (the shekel engine\'s cell). I4-I5 on the native-born; the verdict table a compile datum.')
# ---- piska 108-109 (15:14-16): the stranger's offering; one statute ----
srow(108, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE PROSELYTE ENTERS BY BLOOD; THE FOWL BURNT-OFFERING WHOLLY TO THE FIRE. "If a stranger sojourn among you" (15:14) — the proselyte of the exodus; "throughout your generations" — one who converts now; "he shall offer a fire-offering" — an offering OF BLOOD, not a meal-offering ("thus shall he do" — as you in the desert, by blood); not necessarily a beast\'s as at Exod 24:5 — "for you and for the stranger" (15:16) likens him to you in the requirement, not in the offering\'s specifics; REBBI: Israel entered the covenant by THREE things — circumcision, immersion, the acceptance of an offering — so the proselytes (the exam\'s Keritot 9a; Yevamot 46a-47b); not peace-offerings — "a fire-offering, a sweet savor": which blood-offering goes WHOLLY to the fire? only a fowl burnt-offering (a beast\'s skin reverts to the priests); one bird impossible — "we find no single bird as an offering in the whole Torah": ALL THE BIRD PAIRS ARE HALF BURNT- HALF SIN-OFFERING EXCEPT THE PROSELYTE\'S, wholly to the fire (a lexical census with its proof — Mishnah Kinnim\'s premise); "as you do, thus shall he do" — six logs for a bull, four for a ram, three for a lamb, so for the proselyte (Abba Chanan). The middah: I4-I5 on the offering\'s kind; the census as evidence.')
srow(109, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE CONGREGATION INCLUDES THE WOMEN; ONE STATUTE FOR THE STRANGER — THE FRONTPLATE\'S ACCEPTANCE TOO; ONE TORAH, ONE JUDGMENT = ALL THE COMMANDMENTS. "The congregation" (15:15) — 15:2\'s "the sons of Israel" spoke of men; the congregation brings the women; "one statute for you and the stranger" — proselytes named because the section addressed Israel; "an everlasting statute unto your generations" — in every generation; "as you, thus shall the stranger be BEFORE THE LORD" — Exod 28:38\'s frontplate "for acceptance for them before the LORD" extended to proselytes (the vestments engine\'s acceptance clause read with this seat); "one Torah and one judgment" (15:16) — the proselyte LIKENED TO THE NATIVE-BORN IN ALL THE COMMANDMENTS OF THE TORAH: the ink\'s three "one law" formulas for the stranger in this chapter (15:15 "one statute", 15:16 "one Torah and one judgment", 15:29 "one Torah") beside Exod 12:49, Lev 24:22, Num 9:14 — computed in the ledger\'s ink section. I4-I5; the lexical extension by the doubled formula.')
# ---- piska 110 (15:17-21): the challah ----
srow(110, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'SCRIPTURE VARIED THIS "COMING" — CHALLAH FROM THE MOMENT OF ENTRY; BREAD IS THE FIVE SPECIES; THE GREAT TERUMAH; NOT FROM FLOUR; FROM DOUGH AND FROM BREAD; AS THE THRESHING-FLOOR\'S TERUMAH. (The row on 15:17-20 — the export heads it "15:15-17"; placed by its neighbors 109 on 15:15 and 111 on 15:22 and by its opening "upon your coming to the land whither I bring you there" = 15:18.) R. YISHMAEL: every other "coming" in the Torah reads "and it shall be, when you come" / "when the LORD brings you" (settlement); HERE ALONE "upon your coming" (בְּבֹאֲכֶם, "when you come" — the form\'s one seat in the Torah; computed) — challah devolved AT ONCE on entering the land: THE VARIED FORMULA READ AS LAW (M-23\'s form at a single seat against a formula\'s many — the ink measured); "whither I bring you THERE" — produce from outside brought in is subject (R. Eliezer; R. Akiva exempts — and R. Yehudah records the two REVERSED, each with his verse: "when you eat of the bread of the LAND" against "there"); "bread" here and "bread" at Deut 16:3 (I2, the identity of wording) — the FIVE SPECIES: wheat, barley, rye, oats, spelt (Mishnah Challah 1:1); "you shall separate terumah" (15:19) — the GREAT TERUMAH, since 15:20 already names the challah (the two offerings in two verses); Deut 18:4\'s first-fruits "shall you give" MANDATORY, not optional; not from flour — "the first of your DOUGH" (a chance meal of started dough allowed until rolled or kneaded; after, death for eating untithed — the bracketed Mishnah Challah 3:1 row); if not taken from the dough, taken from the BREAD (15:19 "when you eat of the bread"); R. Akiva: all turns on the CRUST forming in the oven; "as the terumah of the threshing floor, so shall you offer it" (15:20 — the phrase\'s one seat; computed): R. Yoshiyah — challah takes terumah\'s whole law: its measure, its lifting in a hundred and one, its forbidding in a hundred, death and the fifth (Lev 5:16); R. YONATHAN "whispered" — why liken it to the threshing-floor\'s terumah whose measure is unstated, and not to the tithe\'s terumah (Num 18:26) whose tenth is explicit? — answered by the clause\'s own naming: "as the terumah of the THRESHING FLOOR" (the analogy\'s target chosen by the ink, not by the arguer — a middah-governance row; MIDDOT.md). The exam: Mishnah Challah 1-3; Terumot 4-5; the terumah engine at Numbers 18 (OWED forward).')
srow(110, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'PART OF THE DOUGH, NOT ALL; LEKET, SHIKCHAH AND PEAH SUBJECT; TERUMAH-DOUGH AND SECOND-TITHE DOUGH; THE MEASURE — ONE IN TWENTY-FOUR, ONE IN FORTY-EIGHT; THE SABBATICAL AFTERGROWTHS. "OF the first of your dough" (15:21 — the מ- "from" against 15:20\'s bare "the first": the two spellings of the dough-word, plene at 15:20 and with the yod at 15:21 — computed) — part and not all; "the first of your dough" (15:20) INCLUDES leket, shikchah and peah (exempt from tithe yet subject to challah — the a-fortiori from rice and millet refused, and the reverse a-fortiori refused by "bread" = the five species, I2); terumah-dough and second-tithe dough excluded by "challah shall you separate as an offering" — what is separated holy and what remains common (second-tithe dough in Jerusalem subject — the recorded exception); "shall you GIVE to the LORD as an offering" (15:21) — the amount unstated until "give" makes it a GIFT to the priest: A PRIVATE PERSON ONE IN TWENTY-FOUR, A BAKER ONE IN FORTY-EIGHT (the dough\'s size decides the gift; R. Yehudah: generosity decides — never less than a forty-eighth) — Mishnah Challah 2:7\'s row with its two reasons; the feast for one\'s sons, the market-woman, the dough made unclean unwittingly or by force (a forty-eighth) or deliberately (a twenty-fourth, "that the sinner not profit"); R. Shimon b. Yochai: a sixtieth valid without intent; "throughout your generations" — the SABBATICAL AFTERGROWTHS subject (the a-fortoiri chain through leket refuted, the clause deciding); "one who eats of the aftergrowths before its challah is taken is liable to death". I1 refused twice; the measures the data channel\'s (Eruvin 4a).')
# ---- piska 111 (15:22-26): the communal error — idolatry ----
srow(111, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'IDOLATRY DEPARTED FROM THE GENERAL TO TAKE ITS OWN OFFERINGS; "ALL THE COMMANDMENTS" = THE ONE THAT DENIES THEM ALL; "WHICH THE LORD SPOKE TO MOSES" = THE TEN WORDS, MOSES\', THE FOREFATHERS\', THE PROPHETS\'. "If you err and do not do all of these commandments" (15:22): idolatry was inside Lev 4:14\'s general (the congregation\'s bull for every unwitting transgression) and Scripture REMOVED it here — a bull for a BURNT-offering and a goat for a SIN-offering (the changed offerings fix the section\'s subject — I8: the case that departs from the general with a new law; the ink\'s delta against Lev 4:14 computed in the ledger); "all the commandments" — one commandment named by 15:24\'s "done in error", and which? IDOLATRY: he who transgresses ALL casts off the yoke, breaks the covenant, perverts the Torah — so he who transgresses THIS one (Deut 17:2-3 "to destroy His covenant", and "the covenant is nothing other than Torah" — Deut 28:69, a lexical rule with its proof-seat); Rebbi: "ALL" here and "ALL likenesses" at Deut 5:8 (I2); "which the LORD spoke to Moses" — one who acknowledges idolatry DENIES THE TEN COMMANDMENTS (Exod 20:1 "spoke all these words"; Ps 62:12; Jer 23:29), and by 15:23 "all that the LORD commanded you by the hand of Moses" — Moses\' commands; "from the day the LORD commanded" — the forefathers\', from ADAM (Gen 2:15 "and the LORD God commanded the man" — the Eden unit\'s seated first command, the shelf\'s own reading of it); "and onward throughout your generations" — the prophets\': "one who denies idolatry acknowledges the entire Torah" (the exam\'s Horayot 8a; Kiddushin 40a).')
srow(111, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'ONE BULLOCK, ONE GOAT — TWO A-FORTIORIS REFUSED BY THE WORD "ONE"; THE LIBATION IS THE BURNT-OFFERING\'S. "If by the eyes of the congregation it were done in error" (15:24) — the section allotted to idolatry alone; "one young bullock as a burnt-offering" — why "ONE"? else: where the congregation brings no bull for a burnt-offering it brings a bull for a sin-offering (Lev 4:14), so here where it does, how much more a bull for a sin-offering too — REFUSED by "one" (I1 capped by the clause; the parser reads the verse\'s two ones — computed); "with its meal-offering and its libation" — the BURNT-offering\'s, not the sin-offering\'s, by "as ordained" (no libation is ordained for a sin-offering — the libation table of 15:4-11 the ordinance); "and one kid of goats as a sin-offering" — why "one"? else from Yom Kippur\'s two goats where no bull burnt-offering is brought — REFUSED by "one". The verdict table for the compile: idolatry / congregation → a bull OLAH with its libation + one goat CHATAT (Lev 4\'s bull chatat displaced).')
srow(111, 3, 'MATERIAL', 'ATONEMENT FOR ALL THE CONGREGATION — WITHHELD IF ONE TRIBE DID NOT BRING; THE COURT\'S ERROR AND THE PEOPLE\'S DEED; THE TRIBE THAT ERRED (MEIR / YOSHIYAH / SHIMON B. YOCHAI — 1, 12, 2 BULLS); THE MAJORITY AS ALL; WOMEN, PROSELYTES; THE HIGH PRIEST EXCLUDED. "And the priest shall atone for the ENTIRE congregation" (15:25) — one tribe\'s missing offering withholds atonement for all; "for it was unwitting" — not willful; 15:24\'s "by the eyes of the congregation" read as the COURT\'S ruling in error while the people\'s DOING was equated willful with unwitting — refused: "the children of Israel... for it was unwitting"; some willful → not collectively unwitting: "the ENTIRE congregation... unwitting"; "and they have brought their offering": R. MEIR — a tribe that followed its own court\'s error: I might think it brings — no, "THEY" = all the tribes; R. YOSHIYAH — one tribe erred by the court\'s ruling: the OTHER tribes bring because of it — a tribe by its own court liable and the others exempt; by the GREAT court: that tribe a bull and the others TWELVE bulls because of it; R. SHIMON B. YOCHAI — by its own court exempt; by the great court TWO bulls (one for the tribe, one for the court), and for IDOLATRY two bulls and two goats — Mishnah Horayot 1:5\'s three-way table on its verse (the exam; the data channel\'s rows); "the majority of the congregation is reckoned as all"; "a fire-offering" the burnt-offering, "their sin-offering" the goat for idolatry, "their error" the bull of concealment (Lev 4:13-14) — "their sin-offering... for their error": the goats\' procedure LIKE the bull\'s (I3 by the paired nouns); "the entire congregation" (15:26) — the women; "the stranger" — proselytes named because 15:12 addressed Israel; "for to ALL THE PEOPLE it was in error" — EXCLUDES THE HIGH PRIEST, whose bull for the other commandments (Lev 4:3) and Yom Kippur\'s bull where the congregation brings none (Lev 16:3) would give him a bull here by two a-fortioris — both REFUSED by the clause (he brings an individual\'s she-goat, 15:27; piska 112). The exam: Horayot 1-2; Mishnah Horayot 1:5, 2:6.')
# ---- piska 112 (15:27-31): the one soul; the high hand ----
srow(112, 1, 'MATERIAL', 'THE INDIVIDUAL, THE PRINCE AND THE HIGH PRIEST ALIKE — A SHE-GOAT OF THE FIRST YEAR FOR IDOLATRY; "IN ERROR" EXCLUDES THE WILLFUL AND THE DOUBTFUL AND THE ERROR-ABOUT-IDOLATRY; "GOAT" = FIRST YEAR (A PROTOTYPE); "NATIVE-BORN" = PROSELYTES INCLUDED, GENTILES NOT; KARET-FOR-WILLFUL, SIN-OFFERING-FOR-UNWITTING (R. YEHUDAH B. BETEIRA). "And if one soul sin in error" (15:27): for the other commandments the individual brings a ewe-lamb or she-goat, the prince a he-goat, the high priest and the court a bull (Lev 4) — here Scripture REMOVES them to one offering, "a she-goat of the first year" for all three (I8 again; the verdict column collapsed to one row); the subject IDOLATRY by the section\'s subject (R. Yitzchak: the congregation\'s case changed its offerings and is idolatry — so the individual\'s, whose offering changed too: the paired departure as the proof); "in error" — EXCLUDES the willful (the a-fortiori from the light commandments refused); "a she-goat of the first year" — A PROTOTYPE: wherever "goat" is written, of the first year (I3 — Mishnah Parah 1:? / Temurah\'s age rows); "the soul that is unwitting IN SINNING" (15:28) — his willful sins caused the error; EXCLUDES one unwitting as to its BEING idolatry (a church for a synagogue — the shelf\'s own example); "to atone for him" — EXCLUDES DOUBT (whether he bowed to the asherah — the a-fortiori from the light commandments\' suspensive guilt-offering refused: no asham talui for idolatry, Mishnah Keritot 6:3\'s premise); "and he shall be forgiven" — absolutely, as every other "forgiving"; "the native-born among the children of Israel" (15:29) — Lev 23:42\'s "all the native-born" for the sukkah extended to proselytes: A PROTOTYPE — wherever "native-born", proselytes included (the sukkah engine\'s cell touched by reference); variantly — Israelites bring for unwitting idolatry, GENTILES DO NOT (though commanded against it); "one Torah for him who acts unwittingly" — the individual, the prince, the high priest (the two a-fortioris for the high priest\'s bull refused again by this clause); R. YEHUDAH B. BETEIRA: the unwitting act is LIKE idolatry — willful punished by karet (Lev 20:3), unwitting by a sin-offering (Num 15:27) — so EVERY act liable to a sin-offering when unwitting must be one liable to karet when willful: MISHNAH KERITOT 1:2\'S PRINCIPLE ("for these one is liable to karet if willful, a sin-offering if unwitting") STATED ON ITS VERSE (I3, the paradigm from idolatry to the class — the answer sheet\'s premise with its derivation). The exam: Keritot 1; Horayot 2; Shabbat 68b-69a (the error about idolatry).')
srow(112, 2, 'MATERIAL', 'THE HIGH HAND = MANASSEH\'S RIDICULE OF "TRIVIAL" VERSES; SIN AS A STRAND THEN A ROPE; MITZVAH TOWS MITZVAH; "BLASPHEMES" = SCRAPES THE DISH (RESH FOR DALET); KARET = CHILDLESS; THE DESPISER — SADDUCEE, HERETIC, DISTORTER, UNCIRCUMCISED SONS, "NO TORAH FROM HEAVEN" EVEN FOR ONE VERSE OR ONE A-FORTIORI, LEARNS BUT DOES NOT TEACH, IDOLATRY (R. YISHMAEL); "CUT OFF, SHALL BE CUT OFF" — TWO WORLDS (AKIVA) OR THE LANGUAGE OF MEN (YISHMAEL); "ITS INIQUITY IS IN IT" — DEATH DOES NOT ATONE; NOT VISITED ON SONS; THE SAMARITANS REFUTED. "The soul who acts with a high hand" (15:30 — the phrase "with a high hand" the EXODUS\'S OWN at Exod 14:8 and Num 33:3, the ink\'s homograph of posture — computed): MANASSEH b. Hezekiah sitting to ridicule — "He should not have written \'and Reuben went in the days of the wheat harvest\' (Gen 30:14), nor \'and the sister of Lotan was Timna\' (Gen 36:22)" — the shelf\'s own exemplars of the verses a scoffer calls needless, both SEATED in the Genesis units (the mandrakes, the Edomite list — credited by reference); Ps 50:20-21, Isa 5:18 — sin a spider\'s strand at first, a wagon rope at last; REBBI: mitzvah tows mitzvah, transgression transgression (Avot 4:2\'s row); "it is the LORD whom he BLASPHEMES (מְגַדֵּף)" — R. Elazar b. Azaryah: "you scraped the dish and scraped (מגרף) the dish itself" — the resh/dalet pair as the exposition\'s hinge (the letter-shape move on the shelf); Issi b. Akiva: "scraped it all and left nothing"; "that soul shall be cut off" — KARET IS CESSATION (childless — the data channel\'s definition of the sanction); "that soul" — the deliberate; "from the midst of its people" — the people at peace; "the word of the LORD he has despised" (15:31) — the Sadducee; "His commandment he has broken" — the heretic; the distorter of Torah; the breaker of the covenant of the flesh (uncircumcised sons) — R. Elazar HaModai: desecrating the offerings, cheapening the festivals, breaking Abraham\'s covenant — no portion though many mitzvot (Avot 3:11\'s row on this verse); "NO TORAH FROM HEAVEN" — even "all but this one thing Moses said on his own", even "all but this inference, this A-FORTIORI" is "the word of the LORD despised" (the exam\'s Sanhedrin 99a — the tradition sentencing the denial of ONE MIDDAH on this verse: the inference rules themselves under the karet clause); one who learns and does not teach; able and does not (R. Nechemiah); heedless (R. Nathan); R. YISHMAEL: idolatry — "the word of the LORD" = the first commandment, "I am the LORD your God" (Exod 20:2-3); "CUT OFF, SHALL BE CUT OFF" (the doubled infinitive, the pair\'s one seat — computed): R. AKIVA — this world and the world to come; R. YISHMAEL — 15:30 already said "cut off": are there THREE worlds? "that soul shall be cut off" this world, "cut off" the world to come, and the doubling: THE TORAH SPEAKS IN THE LANGUAGE OF MEN — the governance fork on whether a doubled infinitive is expounded, on its classic seat (MIDDOT.md); "its iniquity is in it" — all who die are atoned by death but this one (Ezek 32:27 "their iniquities upon their bones") — unless repented (Deut 32:5 "their blemish" — His children when the blemish is gone); R. Yishmael: not visited on sons — Exod 20:5\'s third and fourth generation LIMITED by "in it" (the Decalogue\'s clause parameterized at this seat); R. Nathan: a good sign — exacted after death (Jer 8:1-2); R. Shimon b. Elazar against the Samaritans\' "the dead do not live": "its iniquity in it" — the soul\'s accounting on the day of judgment. The exam: Sanhedrin 90b, 99a; Keritot 7a-b; Shevuot 13a; Yoma 86a.')
